<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gwenwynwyn ab Owain</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1216</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gwenwynwyn ab Owain was prince of southern Powys from 1195, which was known after him as Powys Wenwynwyn. Son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/owain-cyfeiliog">Owain Cyfeiliog</a>, he tried to lead the Welsh princes against the English but was overshadowed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llywelyn-the-great">Llywelyn the Great</a> of Gwynedd, who seized his lands in 1208. He died in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> in 1216.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gwenwynwyn-ab-owain.jpg" alt="Gwenwynwyn ab Owain" width="320" height="331" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gwenwynwyn ab Owain · PDM-owner · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seal_of_Gwenwynwyn_ab_Owain,.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
